\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Once in royal David's city
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Stood a lowly cattle shed,
\par Where a mother laid her baby
\par In a manger for His bed.
\par Mary was that mother mild,
\par Jesus Christ her little Child.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  He came down to earth from heaven
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Who is God and lord of all.
\par And His shelter was a stable,
\par And His cradle was a stall.
\par With the poor and mean and lowly
\par Lived on earth and Saviour holy.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  And through all His wondrous childhood,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He would honour and obey,
\par Love, and watch the lowly maiden
\par In whose gentle arms He lay.
\par Christian children, all  must be
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Mild, obedient, good as He.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  For He is our childhood's pattern:
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Day by day, like us He grew;
\par He was little, weak, and helpless;
\par  Tears and smiles like us He knew:
\par  And He feeleth for our sadness,
\par  And He shareth in our gladness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  And our eyes at last shall see Him,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Through His own redeeming love;
\par  For the Child so dear and gentle,
\par  Is our Lord in heaven above;
\par  And He leads His children on
\par  To the place where He is gone.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Not in that poor lowly stable,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  With the oxen standing by,
\par  We shall see Him, but in heaven,
\par  Sit at God's right hand on high,
\par  When, like stars, His children crowned
\par \pard      All in white shall wait around.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

